A||N||2||RiceBurner515||Rod Knock? Piston rod or Pushrod?||||1||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||12-29-2000||01:07 PM||||When you have a rod knock, does it mean a piston rod or a pushrod is broke/bent? Also, what are some reasons for a knocking engine?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RiceBurner515||12-29-2000||01:10 PM||||Also, my oil pressure has been kinda figgity lately, is this some kind of symptom of something? How much does Kick Hill sell there engines for? i want to upgrade to a 2.8 or 3.4, i have a 2.5 now 5spd manual.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||12-29-2000||01:33 PM||||if the connecting rod (piston rod) has spun that is USUALLY what the "rod knock" you'll hear.. aka.. Spun a bearing, threw a rod... if a vlave push rod breaks the car will have ONE HELLUVA time running.. and usually won't run at all... 6-8-12s will runn but won't be happy about it... assuming the push rod broke with the valve closed.. if it broke open you'll have to replace the head, valve, piston and whatever else is all mangled to hell.  usually if the oil pressure is crappy it's the cam bearings failing and the rod bearings(piston rod/connecting rod) and it's RARELY the crank bearings... for a few bucks you can get a new set of bearings and ride on thiose for a LONG time.. it'll take about $6 and 6 hours of your time replacing them... GT Bastard has been RAILING on the 2.8 in the SE i swapped bearings in .. it still makes a bit of noise but will happily out run a civic/jettaV6/EscortGT just to name a few.. that was ATLEAST 3000 miles ago... (i put 1800 on them in july! he still tooling around with it)||||reg||1
